feat: make the package publishable

Three things blocked `npm publish`, found by actually packing it.

1. bin pointed at a file that was never built
   package.json declared codeyang-setup -> dist/setup-wizard.js, but
   src/setup-wizard.ts was not in the tsup entry list, so that path did not
   exist. Anyone running `npx codeyang-setup` after install would get ENOENT.
   Added it to the entry map and verified the built binary starts the wizard.

2. files listed a directory that does not exist
   files: ["dist", "codeyangx"] - there is no codeyangx/ directory. Removed,
   and replaced with the docs that are actually worth shipping (README,
   LICENSE, STATUS, QUICKSTART, architecture, api-reference, SECURITY,
   CHANGELOG). No source, no tests, no docs/archive.

3. Package name availability was assumed, not checked
   Verified codeyang, codeyang-cli and codeyang-agent all return 404 from the
   registry (i.e. free). Codeyang keeps its own name.

Verification - packed the tarball, extracted it, and used it from a clean dir:
  28 exports, VERSION 1.1.0, tools=82, envNames=68,
  isPrivateIP(10.0.0.1)=true, isPrivateIP([::1])=true, getTool(Read)=true,
  `node dist/index.js --version` -> CodeYang v1.1.0,
  `node dist/setup-wizard.js` -> wizard starts.
  npm pack: 75 files, 1.0 MB packed / 4.5 MB unpacked.

`npm publish --dry-run` passes; only npm authentication is missing, which
needs the account owner's credentials. Steps are in docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md,
including the note that the local registry is npmmirror (which cannot publish)
so publish must target registry.npmjs.org explicitly.
